  "hit": {
    "_about": "PHYS2 (PH3 phase P2): hit-reaction PARTIAL ragdoll for the LIVING fighters. PRESENTATION ONLY: the 60 Hz Duel sim stays authoritative, nothing here writes sim state, no UnityEngine.Random, no colliders (the proxy bodies are invisible to every physics query). HitReact keeps a collider-less powered copy of the pre-built rig (Scripts/Physics/HitReact.cs): joint drives (spring / damper from ragdoll.json drive + parts gain / damping: body 2 / 0.25, neck + head 1 / 1) chase the animated pose; a landed Hit (ContactRelay) adds a reaction = the V3 dip curve (ease in, hold, recover) on the motors of the row's parts plus V3's impulse at the zone part; per-bone `blend` shares mix the clip's local rotation with the proxy's (Slerp), so the body sways and recovers; parts with share 0 follow their parent's deviation through the hierarchy. Runs in LateUpdate BEFORE FootGround (order -140), so FootGround still plants the feet after the blend. Dead fighters are skipped (RagdollRig takes over). mode: 'stagger' = V3's generic reaction (row 'stagger'); 'zone' = V3 feel-hitreact.json zone rows (head / torso / arms / legs; opt-in in V3 too). Blow class scales the row: light 0.12 impulse / 0.12 dip / 0.2 blend (Dom: tone it down), heavy + counter 1. enabled=false = nothing is created. Keys with $near take the side the blow came from.",
